Repository: https://github.com/AnisB/large_cbt
Revision: 091068c6a8 (2024-07-01, initial commit; the only commit that ever
touched the vendored CBT sources - verified 2026-10-11)
Reference: upstream main checked 2026-10-11; the vendored files below match
that commit byte-for-byte except for the mechanical adaptations listed
under "Divergence". The broader demo (DX12 renderer, shaders, water, moon)
was never vendored.
License: NONE. The upstream repository ships no license file and no license
headers in these sources (GitHub reports license: null as of 2026-10-11),
so the code is used here with no grant beyond fair-use benchmarking. This
is stricter than the libcbt case (dual MIT, see libcbt.LICENSE.txt).

Quarantine: benchmark oracle ONLY (AGENTS.md section 10.2: an upstream
implementation may be bound as an oracle/benchmark baseline). The compiled
objects link exclusively into dev-dependencies of thessa-rcbt-core and
thessa-rcbt-wgpu (benches and hardware tests); no runtime library, binary,
or asset in the workspace links them, and Cargo never propagates a
dev-dependency to downstream crates. No large_cbt code is copied into the
project: domain implementations (bisector pool, compact counters, OCBT
mirror, GPU pipeline) are independent, cite the HPG 2024 paper as primary
source, and document how they differ. Whole-renderer parity with large_cbt
is explicitly disclaimed (docs/22, docs/47).

If upstream publishes a license, adopt it here immediately. If upstream
objects to this use, remove the vendor directory and the ffi binding the
same day; the benches that consume them are not load-bearing for the
product. Options under evaluation: written permission, replacing the
oracle with a clean-room CBT reference.

Vendored for bench-only FFI (upstream files, mechanical adaptations only):
- third_party/large_cbt/cbt.h (upstream abstract CBT base + added virtual
  destructor so the FFI shim can delete through the base pointer)
- third_party/large_cbt/cbt_utility.h (include path flattened)
- third_party/large_cbt/ocbt_128k.h/.cpp (include paths flattened)
- third_party/large_cbt/ocbt_256k.h/.cpp (include paths flattened)
- third_party/large_cbt/ocbt_512k.h/.cpp (include paths flattened)
- third_party/large_cbt/ocbt_1m.h/.cpp (include paths flattened)
- third_party/large_cbt/ocbt_generic.h (include paths flattened; one dead
  line dropped - upstream computes target_bits then recomputes it inline
  in the return, behaviorally identical)
- third_party/large_cbt/graphics/types.h (project-written: fixed-width
  placeholders for the opaque GPU handles the CPU OCBT layout references;
  the upstream header is not vendored)
- third_party/large_cbt/math/operators.h (project-written: only the std
  subset the OCBT code uses; the upstream header is not vendored)
- third_party/large_cbt/tools/security.h (project-written: same assert
  contract, renamed parameters; the upstream header is not vendored)
- third_party/large_cbt/large_cbt_shim.cpp does not exist here; the
  project-owned plain-ABI shim is crates/rcbt-large-ffi/src/large_cbt_shim.cpp

